hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1316","Abdul-Jabbar bin Al-Ala’ and Sa’id bin Abdul-Rahman told us, they said: Sufyan told us, and Ali bin Khashram told us, Ibn Uyaynah said: I said to Amr bin Dinar: Did you hear Jabir bin Abdullah say: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to a man who passed by shares in... The mosque: “Hold its blades.” He said: Yes, this is the hadith of Al-Makhzoumi."
"1317","Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman narrated to us, Shuaib narrated to us, Al-Layth narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: He ordered a man who was giving arrows in charity in the mosque not to pass by it unless he was holding its arrows.”"
